# SFA i18n (English · Hindi · Hinglish)

## Supported languages
| Code | Language |
|------|----------|
| `en` | English |
| `hi` | Hindi (Devanagari) |
| `hinglish` | Hinglish (Roman script mix) |

## MUST
- Add user-visible strings to `packages/shared-i18n` — **all 3 languages in the same PR**
- Web: use `useI18n()` from `apps/web/src/i18n/I18nProvider.tsx` — never inline labels in JSX
- API user-facing errors: `apiTranslate(key, language)` via `X-App-Language` header
- Include i18n parity tests (`shared-i18n`) and feature tests when adding strings
- Show `LanguageSwitcher` on auth/shell screens (already wired in Phase 0)

## MUST NOT
- Hardcode English-only copy in React components or NestJS exceptions
- Add a string to only one language file
- Bypass `MessageKey` typing with raw strings in `t()`

## New feature checklist
1. Define keys in `packages/shared-i18n/src/messages/`
2. Add en + hi + hinglish translations
3. Wire web with `t('your.key')`
4. Wire API errors with language param where users see the message
5. Run `pnpm --filter @synchem-sfa/shared-i18n test`
